1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,880
A single spark can start a fire in seconds.

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:08,960
What should you do?

3
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:14,350
Fire needs three elements:
fuel, oxygen and heat.

4
00:00:14,610 --> 00:00:16,850
Without all three, it cannot start.

5
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,200
Keep combustibles stored safely,

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:24,440
don't overload electrical outlets,
and report electrical faults immediately.

7
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:30,010
If you discover a fire, warn others, raise the alarm,
and call your local emergency number.

8
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:33,990
If the fire is small, you're trained,
and your escape route is clear,

9
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,890
you may use the right extinguisher.

10
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,430
Pull the pin. Aim at the base.

11
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:41,260
Squeeze. And sweep side to side.

12
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:45,820
If the fire spreads, or it's unsafe,
evacuate immediately.

13
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:49,440
Stay low if there's smoke.
Never use elevators.

14
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,040
Follow the escape route.

15
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:54,010
Go to the assembly point
and report for the headcount.

16
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:57,900
Learn your escape route,
and your extinguisher location, today.
